{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-20T04:44:11.213Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"f719b3080f29d4118076bddd","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.329","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1759"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1759: strict health accepts a merge fence from an enclosing repository for a separate linked worktree"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Reported in GH-1759 against 2026.11.19. auditMergeAttributeFence (src/sdk/merge/install.ts) looks for the managed .gitattributes block by walking filesystem parents of the tracker root up to eight levels, and it does not stop at the active Git worktree root. When a linked worktree of one repository is checked out inside a different repository that has a stale matching fence, the walk finds the outer file. Git never reads attributes above its own top level, so git check-attr reports merge unspecified, yet pm health --strict-exit reports ok with no warnings and exits 0. pm validate and the workspace position read use the same audit. The fix bounds the walk at the active Git worktree root, keeping support for several trackers inside one repository (pm-kynkl8) and the per-worktree driver isolation of GH-1306 (pm-c1dwbt)."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:merge","false-success","gh:1759","health","merge-fence","worktree"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-20T04:44:11.213Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-20T04:44:11.213Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":90},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"A matching managed fence in a .gitattributes above the active Git worktree root never counts: strict health reports merge_fence_missing and exits 1 for a linked worktree with no own fence; An installed fence at the linked worktree root still passes strict health, and a fence inside the same repository between the root and the tracker still counts; pm validate and the workspace position read use the same bounded audit; a tracker outside any Git repository keeps today's bounded walk; A real-Git regression test reproduces the GH-1759 layout and checks both git check-attr and strict health"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-o2kc"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Merge-fence evidence is bounded to the active Git worktree, so a fence Git cannot apply never satisfies strict health."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"A stale matching fence in an enclosing, unrelated repository makes strict health report ok, zero warnings and exit 0 while git check-attr reports merge unspecified."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"merge"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-c1dwbt","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-20T04:44:11.213Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-kynkl8","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-20T04:44:11.213Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"ac84c2894a7a76c6bbf6350d1